WEBVTT

00:00:11.970 --> 00:00:13.680
We're going back to the others.

00:00:13.760 --> 00:00:15.550
We have to warn them about the bats.

00:00:15.640 --> 00:00:17.350
You expect us to trust you?

00:00:17.430 --> 00:00:19.220
You dirty bastards kidnapped one of ours!

00:00:19.310 --> 00:00:22.180
You used a child as a guinea pig!
You have no right to talk!

00:00:24.270 --> 00:00:27.480
-Ms. Hana, I'm going to stay here.
-Are you sure, Mr. Aramaki?

00:00:28.070 --> 00:00:29.480
The dogs still need to rest.

00:00:29.570 --> 00:00:31.490
I'll keep watch over them and Momota.

00:00:31.570 --> 00:00:33.070
Ango, I'll go with her.

00:00:33.650 --> 00:00:35.490
Koruri is probably
with the rest of their group.

00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:37.160
If you're going to go with her,

00:00:37.780 --> 00:00:40.490
then both of you remember
that I will still be here.

00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:45.330
If you do anything to the others,
I won't hesitate to take action.

00:00:45.920 --> 00:00:46.920
All right.

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:49.210
I'm going, then.
But I promise I'll come back.

00:00:49.710 --> 00:00:50.840
Stay safe.

00:00:50.960 --> 00:00:52.710
Ban! Is Ban in there with you?

00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:54.720
-Koruri. Where have you--
-Ban.

00:00:55.180 --> 00:00:57.180
Grab the first-aid kit!

00:00:57.260 --> 00:00:59.470
-We'll fly tandem on the glider!
-What?

00:02:32.770 --> 00:02:34.780
LESSER HEAT

00:02:35.570 --> 00:02:36.490
That hurts.

00:02:37.070 --> 00:02:38.070
Ban...

00:02:38.150 --> 00:02:40.950
This brings back memories
of our final test, right?

00:02:43.700 --> 00:02:45.620
We need to wash their wounds
with clean water.

00:02:45.870 --> 00:02:46.950
I'm on it.

00:02:48.830 --> 00:02:50.250
Disinfect the larger wounds first.

00:02:50.330 --> 00:02:51.170
Right.

00:03:01.550 --> 00:03:02.510
How far along are you?

00:03:04.050 --> 00:03:05.640
I'm not really sure.

00:03:06.680 --> 00:03:08.100
Maybe four months?

00:03:09.230 --> 00:03:10.890
How long has it been
since you woke up here?

00:03:10.980 --> 00:03:12.270
Just about three years.

00:03:14.020 --> 00:03:15.860
-Then you should be okay.
-What?

00:03:15.940 --> 00:03:18.150
Your body has adapted to this environment.

00:03:18.240 --> 00:03:19.150
What do you mean?

00:03:19.240 --> 00:03:23.160
Your body determined that it was okay
to have a baby here.

00:03:24.160 --> 00:03:25.530
That's why you got pregnant.

00:03:26.330 --> 00:03:27.160
I see.

00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:31.960
Thanks.

00:03:32.170 --> 00:03:34.000
I was starting to think
you weren't coming back.

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:34.920
Sorry.

00:03:37.500 --> 00:03:38.920
You're hurt, too.

00:03:39.550 --> 00:03:40.420
Let me see.

00:03:43.010 --> 00:03:46.180
Akiwo, we need to get out of here.
Those bats will be back.

00:03:46.470 --> 00:03:48.310
No place around here is safe.

00:03:48.970 --> 00:03:50.060
They can fly, you know.

00:03:50.140 --> 00:03:51.060
"Bats"?

00:03:51.690 --> 00:03:53.150
Excuse me...

00:03:53.440 --> 00:03:55.730
Oh, sorry. My name is Haru.

00:03:56.440 --> 00:03:57.400
I'm Koruri.

00:03:57.480 --> 00:04:00.860
Well, I want you to help us
get rid of those bats.

00:04:01.530 --> 00:04:02.990
Can we actually succeed?

00:04:03.070 --> 00:04:04.160
Yes.

00:04:04.240 --> 00:04:06.700
You and the others chase the bats
out of their nest.

00:04:06.950 --> 00:04:09.370
Then I'll lure them into the charcoal pit.

00:04:09.450 --> 00:04:11.000
"Charcoal pit"?

00:04:11.500 --> 00:04:13.330
Sounds echo in there.

00:04:13.500 --> 00:04:14.500
I get it.

00:04:14.580 --> 00:04:17.130
That will interfere with
the bats' echolocation.

00:04:17.710 --> 00:04:20.130
The only problem is how we're going to
draw them all out.

00:04:20.210 --> 00:04:22.050
"Counter a ranging rook from the side.

00:04:22.130 --> 00:04:24.590
Remove an imposing knight with haste..."
is what I would say.

00:04:24.800 --> 00:04:25.680
Who's there?

00:04:26.300 --> 00:04:29.510
I was trying to come back,
but those freaky bats stopped me.

00:04:29.600 --> 00:04:30.470
Sakuya?

00:04:30.560 --> 00:04:32.980
What were those weird things
you just said?

00:04:33.060 --> 00:04:34.640
They're Japanese chess proverbs.

00:04:34.730 --> 00:04:36.940
"Japanese chess"? What the hell is that?

00:04:37.940 --> 00:04:39.400
What? You've never heard of it?

00:04:40.030 --> 00:04:44.280
In other words, the best way to deal with
the bats would be to smoke them all out.

00:04:45.910 --> 00:04:48.370
<i>I took a quick look.
There are 18 entrances.</i>

00:04:48.780 --> 00:04:50.830
<i>I've more or less figured out the layout</i>

00:04:50.910 --> 00:04:52.790
<i>based on how long it takes
for them to leave.</i>

00:04:52.870 --> 00:04:57.080
<i>To force them all out of one opening,
we'll smoke each one in an order.</i>

00:05:04.670 --> 00:05:06.800
Koruri, they're on the move.

00:05:16.270 --> 00:05:18.270
<i>This time, things will be different.</i>

00:05:21.860 --> 00:05:23.030
Your prey is over there.

00:05:50.300 --> 00:05:52.310
So the hunters become the hunted?

00:05:53.890 --> 00:05:55.600
That includes us.

00:05:56.180 --> 00:05:58.650
What was that song you just played?

00:05:59.230 --> 00:06:02.230
Johann Strauss II's "Die Fledermaus."

00:06:03.820 --> 00:06:06.360
Haru! I'm so glad you're all right.

00:06:06.990 --> 00:06:09.110
Yes, I'm totally fine. Welcome back.

00:06:09.700 --> 00:06:11.320
Tell me, who exactly are you?

00:06:11.410 --> 00:06:12.620
That voice.

00:06:13.120 --> 00:06:15.080
You're the one who killed Mr. Izayoi.

00:06:15.660 --> 00:06:18.460
We were able to take care of the bats,
thanks to Haru's help.

00:06:20.790 --> 00:06:22.500
Wow! You really got them good!

00:06:22.590 --> 00:06:24.300
We should be safe for the time being.

00:06:24.880 --> 00:06:25.960
They'll attack again.

00:06:26.210 --> 00:06:27.630
This couldn't have been all of them.

00:06:27.880 --> 00:06:29.010
We've got no choice.

00:06:29.300 --> 00:06:33.140
Taking care of the civilians
is part of our duty, after all.

00:06:33.680 --> 00:06:35.270
Right, Ango?

00:06:35.850 --> 00:06:37.060
Right.

00:06:38.640 --> 00:06:41.520
Do you have a gun, too?

00:06:41.650 --> 00:06:42.610
I do.

00:06:43.110 --> 00:06:45.030
But I don't carry it around all the time.

00:06:45.860 --> 00:06:47.070
Mr. Aramaki!

00:06:49.950 --> 00:06:50.910
Ms. Hana!

00:06:51.990 --> 00:06:53.070
And the others!

00:06:54.410 --> 00:06:57.000
Mr. Aramaki, they didn't do anything
to you or Momota, did they?

00:06:57.370 --> 00:06:59.330
No, but why did you all come here?

00:06:59.910 --> 00:07:01.170
He's the one who suggested it.

00:07:01.540 --> 00:07:04.040
He said it would be best
if we all live here together.

00:07:04.840 --> 00:07:08.210
Camping in the danger of the wild,
or with a bunch of murderers.

00:07:08.510 --> 00:07:10.130
It's a choice between two evils.

00:07:10.720 --> 00:07:13.850
You've got weapons and extraordinary
knowledge and skills.

00:07:13.970 --> 00:07:15.350
Who exactly are you?

00:07:15.430 --> 00:07:16.970
I would like to know that as well.

00:07:17.060 --> 00:07:18.680
Why are we civilians to you?

00:07:19.270 --> 00:07:21.810
What exactly differentiates us
from all of you?

00:07:24.020 --> 00:07:27.110
We were raised to survive here.

00:07:28.860 --> 00:07:29.860
<i>Is this the future?</i>

00:07:29.950 --> 00:07:32.820
Or are you just a bunch of kidnappers?

00:07:32.910 --> 00:07:34.780
The future, probably.

00:07:35.700 --> 00:07:38.370
-Do you know what's going on?
-My grandparents explained it to me.

00:07:39.330 --> 00:07:41.250
So our families could have told us.

00:07:41.670 --> 00:07:43.380
Hard to believe they would tell this brat.

00:07:43.460 --> 00:07:44.500
I'm not a brat.

00:07:45.000 --> 00:07:47.050
I was told I would be in Team Spring.

00:07:47.130 --> 00:07:48.380
Are you all part of it?

00:07:48.460 --> 00:07:51.010
No, we're from Team Summer B.

00:07:51.550 --> 00:07:54.140
Do you remember what you said last night?

00:07:54.680 --> 00:07:57.510
There's a girl named
Hotaru Kusakari on our team.

00:07:57.600 --> 00:08:00.140
She's about the same age as you,
and looks very similar.

00:08:01.230 --> 00:08:04.020
Our family is old.
Its roots go back to the Heian period.

00:08:04.350 --> 00:08:06.520
I'm the heiress of the main family.

00:08:06.980 --> 00:08:08.780
Hotaru is a cousin from a branch family.

00:08:13.660 --> 00:08:18.030
Since we were young, there have been times
when we could feel each other.

00:08:18.700 --> 00:08:22.370
Warmth, pain, sadness, injuries,
all sorts of things.

00:08:23.830 --> 00:08:27.000
It's not all the time,
and it usually comes very suddenly.

00:08:27.750 --> 00:08:29.000
Like what happened last night.

00:08:29.880 --> 00:08:31.920
Hotaru is on the verge of death.

00:08:32.510 --> 00:08:34.550
She is dying very slowly.

00:08:39.560 --> 00:08:41.560
You're very clumsy, Ms. Natsu.

00:08:43.100 --> 00:08:45.480
Did you make my bed for me?

00:08:45.560 --> 00:08:47.900
Oh, not yet. I'm not done with this yet.

00:08:48.610 --> 00:08:51.530
I may start feeling sick again
at any moment.

00:08:51.780 --> 00:08:53.110
You're not being very considerate.

00:08:53.450 --> 00:08:55.240
Or are you just incompetent?

00:08:55.320 --> 00:08:58.740
If you were one of our servants,
you would be fired right away.

00:08:59.410 --> 00:09:01.750
Actually,
I doubt we would have even hired you.

00:09:02.450 --> 00:09:04.620
I bet you're hopeless in society.

00:09:04.710 --> 00:09:06.920
I guess it's a good thing
you could come here.

00:09:07.750 --> 00:09:09.540
Bring me a fresh change of clothes.

00:09:10.250 --> 00:09:12.760
I can't believe her.
She's still so childish at her age.

00:09:13.050 --> 00:09:16.010
I'm guessing you bullied
those "servants" of yours pretty often.

00:09:16.630 --> 00:09:18.680
You seem like a miserable kid.

00:09:18.760 --> 00:09:20.890
You get through life by appraising others.

00:09:21.350 --> 00:09:23.140
Who's an ally? Who's an enemy?

00:09:23.220 --> 00:09:26.270
Who's a leader? Who will keep you safe?

00:09:26.520 --> 00:09:28.690
Who can you trample on?

00:09:29.520 --> 00:09:32.400
Just so you know, you can't bully her.

00:09:32.610 --> 00:09:34.070
She's my prey.

00:09:35.320 --> 00:09:36.200
What's so funny?

00:09:36.530 --> 00:09:37.780
You're just like a child.

00:09:37.950 --> 00:09:39.200
Do you have a crush on her?

00:09:41.910 --> 00:09:44.120
She got the better of me because of you!

00:09:44.200 --> 00:09:45.910
Why would I have a crush on you?

00:09:46.210 --> 00:09:47.210
What?

00:09:50.040 --> 00:09:51.670
So you were an architect.

00:09:51.800 --> 00:09:53.510
Then follow my orders from now on.

00:09:53.590 --> 00:09:54.590
No, thanks.

00:09:55.090 --> 00:09:58.470
I've already got plenty of experience,
so I would rather you just shoved off.

00:09:58.970 --> 00:10:01.430
Regardless of how you feel,
you'll be taking orders from me.

00:10:01.510 --> 00:10:02.430
No way.

00:10:02.510 --> 00:10:05.850
So, you're a Japanese <i>ama</i> diver.
Do you know much about sea life?

00:10:06.140 --> 00:10:07.480
Have you seen a poisonous octopus?

00:10:07.560 --> 00:10:10.730
Nobody is better than me
when it comes to stuff like that.

00:10:11.440 --> 00:10:13.480
Hey, you. Hana. What's your specialty?

00:10:14.110 --> 00:10:17.360
What? Oh, rock climbing
and pretty much any outdoor activity.

00:10:17.450 --> 00:10:18.910
Those aren't specialties.

00:10:19.200 --> 00:10:21.740
That's the bare minimum. What else?

00:10:23.160 --> 00:10:24.200
Nothing?

00:10:24.410 --> 00:10:25.540
Then you're untalented.

00:10:25.830 --> 00:10:27.960
You'll do jobs that anyone is capable of.

00:10:29.420 --> 00:10:30.960
Hey, you. Haru.

00:10:31.250 --> 00:10:32.790
Listen. Don't play any music.

00:10:33.170 --> 00:10:34.550
We don't want to hear it.

00:10:35.050 --> 00:10:38.380
And furthermore, don't even think
about getting friendly with Koruri.

00:10:39.930 --> 00:10:41.930
Those without a specialty
get stuck on toilet duty.

00:10:42.510 --> 00:10:43.640
Mix it up.

00:10:43.810 --> 00:10:45.520
Mix it all up and turn it into fertilizer.

00:10:45.600 --> 00:10:47.060
Hey, Plain Jane.

00:10:47.520 --> 00:10:49.480
When you're done there,
go and chop some wood.

00:10:52.150 --> 00:10:53.820
"Plain, with no specialties..."

00:10:54.690 --> 00:10:56.440
Nobody has ever told me that before.

00:10:58.320 --> 00:10:59.150
Haru?

00:10:59.700 --> 00:11:03.370
"You're just as plain, so you get to do
the heavy lifting," was what I was told.

00:11:05.580 --> 00:11:08.000
I told you! The three-point technique!

00:11:08.080 --> 00:11:09.750
Don't overlook your foothold!

00:11:13.380 --> 00:11:14.290
Momota?

00:11:14.880 --> 00:11:16.050
Ms. Hana...

00:11:16.130 --> 00:11:18.300
What are you doing to Momota?

00:11:18.380 --> 00:11:22.300
Teaching him how to be useful
so that he can survive in this world.

00:11:23.090 --> 00:11:25.890
Providing you all with training was
one of the duties we were given.

00:11:27.930 --> 00:11:29.810
You've got one week to learn how to climb!

00:11:29.890 --> 00:11:31.060
Are you kidding?

00:11:31.140 --> 00:11:32.520
That's a Friends SLCD, isn't it?

00:11:33.190 --> 00:11:35.110
My father used to have the same model.

00:11:35.570 --> 00:11:37.730
Although most people use
a Camalot these days.

00:11:38.110 --> 00:11:40.860
Do you have a set
of the most recent post-C4 version?

00:11:42.240 --> 00:11:43.450
"C4"?

00:11:44.450 --> 00:11:46.450
What? That harness doesn't look like

00:11:46.530 --> 00:11:48.240
-the most recent model.
-What?

00:11:48.330 --> 00:11:50.750
I've done gliding
a few times myself, actually.

00:11:50.830 --> 00:11:54.040
Now that I look at it,
this a pretty old model.

00:11:55.460 --> 00:11:57.250
A "Camalot C4"?

00:11:57.750 --> 00:12:00.090
What the hell is a C4?
I've never even heard of that.

00:12:00.170 --> 00:12:02.340
They told me my equipment
was out of date, too.

00:12:02.430 --> 00:12:03.800
Let me get this straight.

00:12:04.140 --> 00:12:06.600
That means
we were put to sleep earlier than them.

00:12:06.760 --> 00:12:08.220
Yes, most likely.

00:12:08.310 --> 00:12:11.810
How the hell are we outdated?
We were the cream of the crop!

00:12:12.230 --> 00:12:14.440
We were raised to be
the absolute best, weren't we?

00:12:18.070 --> 00:12:19.860
Are you going to build something here?

00:12:20.530 --> 00:12:22.320
Well, just a small hut.

00:12:23.070 --> 00:12:25.070
Kurumi and Ryuusei need space
to themselves, right?

00:12:25.660 --> 00:12:29.080
Does this mean that you're no longer
opposed to them having the baby?

00:12:29.540 --> 00:12:30.910
I'm still annoyed by it.

00:12:31.000 --> 00:12:35.040
And my deep hatred for those
who sent us here hasn't faded at all.

00:12:35.330 --> 00:12:37.710
But I no longer feel like I'm trapped.

00:12:38.040 --> 00:12:39.090
I'm sorry.

00:12:39.710 --> 00:12:41.880
I'm not trying to criticize you.

00:12:42.670 --> 00:12:46.470
I think it's perfectly natural for
a parent to want their child to survive.

00:12:47.140 --> 00:12:49.760
To be honest, I don't know how to feel.

00:12:50.310 --> 00:12:53.180
I knew my father
as an ordinary government worker,

00:12:53.690 --> 00:12:56.480
and my mother as an ordinary housewife.

00:12:57.230 --> 00:13:00.650
As it turns out,
I didn't really know either of them.

00:13:07.490 --> 00:13:09.950
It should be fine
if I play this far from the village.

00:13:10.240 --> 00:13:12.540
It's dangerous to walk around
the forest by yourself.

00:13:14.540 --> 00:13:16.080
Is that why you followed me?

00:13:16.500 --> 00:13:17.380
Yes.

00:13:18.170 --> 00:13:21.880
That Ango guy warned me
not to get friendly with you.

00:13:22.630 --> 00:13:25.300
So what's his deal?
Is he your brother? Or your boyfriend?

00:13:25.720 --> 00:13:27.390
Neither. He's just a friend.

00:13:29.100 --> 00:13:31.140
Then I don't need to listen to him, do I?

00:13:33.220 --> 00:13:37.940
I've always wanted to play Debussy's
"Clair de Lune" under the moonlight.

00:14:04.050 --> 00:14:05.210
-Haru!
-I thought I told you

00:14:05.300 --> 00:14:07.220
-to keep away from Koruri!
-Cut it out!

00:14:08.300 --> 00:14:09.840
Ango!

00:14:10.430 --> 00:14:11.850
Haru didn't do anything wrong!

00:14:12.430 --> 00:14:15.850
I knew it was dangerous for us to
sleep in the forest without telling you.

00:14:16.600 --> 00:14:18.230
I'm sorry for worrying you.

00:14:19.560 --> 00:14:21.860
You know that's not what this is about.

00:14:21.940 --> 00:14:23.150
Then what is it about?

00:14:23.650 --> 00:14:25.360
What has made you so angry, Ango?

00:14:25.440 --> 00:14:27.740
Can't I become friends with Haru?

00:14:28.240 --> 00:14:30.370
Why? Is it because he's from another team?

00:14:30.990 --> 00:14:32.870
Why do you get to decide that, Ango?

00:14:37.960 --> 00:14:40.380
I'm going to check the water supply.

00:14:43.960 --> 00:14:46.380
This isn't good.
The water level is starting to drop.

00:14:46.710 --> 00:14:49.720
The rocks are still wet, though,
which means it's dropping fast.

00:14:49.800 --> 00:14:51.180
The dry season is coming.

00:14:51.260 --> 00:14:55.560
When it hits, wetlands and small rivers
are sure to dry up.

00:14:56.220 --> 00:14:59.390
Plants will wither
and most animals will enter hibernation.

00:15:00.560 --> 00:15:01.900
Let's head for the next spot.

00:15:03.110 --> 00:15:04.980
Something reeks around here.

00:15:07.570 --> 00:15:08.990
It's already a muddy swamp.

00:15:12.450 --> 00:15:14.330
Be careful. It's deeper than it looks.

00:15:15.330 --> 00:15:16.240
What do we do?

00:15:16.870 --> 00:15:18.160
Go even further?

00:15:18.250 --> 00:15:20.790
No. There's no point if it's too far away.

00:15:21.330 --> 00:15:23.710
It's better for us
to make a reservoir of our own now.

00:15:24.790 --> 00:15:25.750
I agree.

00:15:29.970 --> 00:15:32.640
This branch is hollow inside,
so it makes a unique sound.

00:15:33.340 --> 00:15:35.560
Maybe I'm more inclined
to percussion instruments.

00:15:35.640 --> 00:15:36.510
I should ask Koruri--

00:15:40.940 --> 00:15:43.310
Hey! Has anybody seen Haru?

00:15:43.480 --> 00:15:45.440
He was with us until a few minutes ago.

00:15:45.520 --> 00:15:46.360
No clue.

00:15:49.360 --> 00:15:50.610
<i>That's weird.</i>

00:15:51.400 --> 00:15:54.120
<i>Shouldn't he suspect Haru
of meeting with Koruri in secret again?</i>

00:15:55.450 --> 00:15:56.780
I'm going to look for him!

00:15:57.700 --> 00:15:58.660
I'll go with you.

00:16:01.250 --> 00:16:02.330
Haru!

00:16:02.540 --> 00:16:04.790
Haru! Where are you?

00:16:05.210 --> 00:16:07.840
Haru!

00:16:14.140 --> 00:16:15.600
Haru!

00:16:22.520 --> 00:16:25.270
Someone suddenly hit me from behind.

00:16:25.810 --> 00:16:27.270
Keep your hands off Haru!

00:16:27.360 --> 00:16:30.030
Don't make false accusations.
I haven't done anything.

00:16:30.110 --> 00:16:32.240
Ms. Hana. That's enough from both of you!

00:16:32.320 --> 00:16:33.450
Hey, hold on a second.

00:16:34.490 --> 00:16:37.370
That knife of yours, I've been curious
about it since I've seen it before.

00:16:37.780 --> 00:16:39.740
That's the exact same knife that we carry.

00:16:39.830 --> 00:16:41.580
Why do you have one?

00:16:41.660 --> 00:16:43.210
This isn't actually mine.

00:16:43.290 --> 00:16:44.920
It's one my father used to have.

00:16:45.830 --> 00:16:47.420
Ango, put the gun away.

00:16:47.920 --> 00:16:48.840
Ryo?

00:16:48.920 --> 00:16:51.670
They have the same
mark of the sun on them.

00:16:51.760 --> 00:16:53.170
A coincidence?

00:16:53.260 --> 00:16:56.180
Impossible. These were specially made
by the Japanese government.

00:16:56.260 --> 00:16:58.680
So what was your father's name?

00:16:59.390 --> 00:17:02.180
Takashi Sugurono. What about it?

00:17:03.560 --> 00:17:04.480
Nijiko?

00:17:05.100 --> 00:17:06.650
Professor Takashi's full name was...

00:17:07.060 --> 00:17:08.480
Takashi Sugurono.

00:17:10.570 --> 00:17:12.740
Professor Takashi was at the facility
we were raised in.

00:17:12.820 --> 00:17:13.860
He taught us.

00:17:14.400 --> 00:17:17.490
He was one of the main staff members
of the 7SEEDS Project.

00:17:17.570 --> 00:17:19.370
My dad wasn't a professor!

00:17:19.660 --> 00:17:22.790
He and my mother both died
in the Ryugu Shelter.

00:17:24.120 --> 00:17:26.540
Professor... Takashi...

00:17:26.620 --> 00:17:29.840
Professor Takashi said that
he would have a child next year!

00:17:29.960 --> 00:17:31.750
Was that you?

00:17:31.840 --> 00:17:35.300
You must have been born
after we were put to sleep, right?

00:17:35.380 --> 00:17:37.220
That can't be. My dad was...

00:17:37.300 --> 00:17:39.760
Your father made a hobby
out of killing people!

00:17:40.300 --> 00:17:41.930
You were never meant to be here.

00:17:42.850 --> 00:17:45.310
But he still put you here without testing.

00:17:45.890 --> 00:17:48.310
He only did it because you're his child!

00:17:48.400 --> 00:17:50.980
You didn't go through what we did!
What Shigeru did!

00:17:51.400 --> 00:17:53.480
He let you in without traversing
that cursed mountain!

00:17:55.240 --> 00:17:56.490
You're all scum...

00:17:56.570 --> 00:17:59.410
You and Professor Takashi...

00:17:59.570 --> 00:18:01.580
You're all scum!

00:18:08.580 --> 00:18:11.000
All of you children are the chosen ones.

00:18:11.090 --> 00:18:14.760
You were born from carefully selected
eggs and sperm.

00:18:14.840 --> 00:18:16.260
Each of you is special.

00:18:16.340 --> 00:18:17.840
Why are you special?

00:18:18.260 --> 00:18:20.510
Because you all have a duty to uphold.

00:18:20.600 --> 00:18:23.510
<i>You must train your bodies and your minds</i>

00:18:23.600 --> 00:18:26.520
<i>in order to become perfect humans.</i>

00:18:26.600 --> 00:18:32.020
<i>You must have the strength and knowledge
necessary to survive in any environment.</i>

00:18:32.110 --> 00:18:35.030
Anyone who can't keep up
will be immediately rejected.

00:18:35.110 --> 00:18:40.780
Listen! You are the chosen few
who will ride upon Noah's Ark!

00:18:40.870 --> 00:18:43.580
Shigeru, I haven't gotten your report.

00:18:43.660 --> 00:18:45.870
If you forgot it,
go to your room and get it.

00:18:46.000 --> 00:18:47.870
I'm sorry. I've been tired...

00:18:47.960 --> 00:18:49.830
I mean, I didn't know what to write.

00:18:50.210 --> 00:18:55.460
Professor, Shigeru has been training
every day to climb the west cliff, so--

00:18:56.170 --> 00:18:58.590
-Ango!
-Don't make excuses!

00:18:59.760 --> 00:19:01.510
<i>Shigeru!</i>

00:19:02.090 --> 00:19:02.970
Wake up.

00:19:04.220 --> 00:19:05.510
It's time for training.

00:19:06.850 --> 00:19:10.100
Slowly. Be careful. You're almost there.

00:19:10.270 --> 00:19:12.520
Nice. Grab hold with your right hand.

00:19:13.230 --> 00:19:16.610
<i>I came to realize that Shigeru was
always by my side.</i>

00:19:17.490 --> 00:19:20.280
I keep telling you
not to stretch your whole body like that.

00:19:20.360 --> 00:19:24.030
Remember the three-point technique?
Don't overlook your foothold.

00:19:26.620 --> 00:19:28.000
-Shigeru!
-Shigeru did it!

00:19:30.080 --> 00:19:32.960
<i>Shigeru and I will be together forever.</i>

00:19:33.420 --> 00:19:35.840
<i>I swear, we'll be part of the seven
who will go to the future.</i>

00:19:37.050 --> 00:19:38.840
<i>We all grew up together.</i>

00:19:43.050 --> 00:19:44.470
Ango is a shoo-in for the team.

00:19:44.550 --> 00:19:45.850
Of course, I am.

00:19:45.930 --> 00:19:47.930
Yes. You'll make it for sure, Ango.

00:19:48.270 --> 00:19:50.850
Hold up, Shigeru.
Don't talk like you won't be chosen.

00:19:50.940 --> 00:19:53.270
Oh, yes. I'll do my best.

00:19:53.350 --> 00:19:55.440
Don't forget about us.
We'll be picked, too.

00:19:55.520 --> 00:19:56.480
My color is red.

00:19:56.570 --> 00:19:57.440
And mine is yellow.

00:19:57.530 --> 00:19:58.690
And I'm blue.

00:19:58.900 --> 00:20:00.780
We made these matching
friendship bracelets.

00:20:01.780 --> 00:20:03.410
Quit making so much racket.

00:20:04.070 --> 00:20:04.910
Ryo...

00:20:04.990 --> 00:20:07.950
Only the best of us are actually
going to be picked.

00:20:08.450 --> 00:20:09.750
Like me.

00:20:10.710 --> 00:20:13.250
<i>We were told seven of us
would be chosen at the age of 17...</i>

00:20:13.920 --> 00:20:16.750
<i>because humanity faced extinction.</i>

00:20:18.920 --> 00:20:24.050
<i>The chosen seven would be put into
cryosleep during the impending cataclysm.</i>

00:20:24.760 --> 00:20:28.890
<i>They would awaken in the future
and create a new history for humanity.</i>

00:20:38.440 --> 00:20:39.440
Got them.

00:20:42.610 --> 00:20:43.990
Hey! That was a human, Ryo!

00:20:44.070 --> 00:20:45.320
He was holding a knife.

00:20:45.570 --> 00:20:46.990
What about the child before that?

00:20:47.200 --> 00:20:48.740
It had contracted a contagious virus.

00:20:48.830 --> 00:20:51.330
How can you shoot a sick person?
You can't make that call.

00:20:51.410 --> 00:20:54.420
Idiot. We have to prepare
for a desolate future.

00:20:54.870 --> 00:20:57.040
I won't hesitate to shoot.
Not even for a second.

00:21:02.170 --> 00:21:03.380
Nobara...

00:21:09.810 --> 00:21:11.180
I'll write you letters...

00:21:11.770 --> 00:21:13.480
and I won't ever remove this bracelet.

00:21:13.680 --> 00:21:14.810
Do your best, everyone!

00:21:15.390 --> 00:21:17.060
-Nobara!
-Nobara!

00:21:17.940 --> 00:21:19.570
Good luck, you guys!

00:21:20.110 --> 00:21:22.400
Best of luck to you too, Nobara!

00:21:22.900 --> 00:21:24.280
Keep in touch!

00:21:26.740 --> 00:21:28.990
We haven't heard anything from Nobara
since she left.

00:21:29.490 --> 00:21:31.290
I wanted to hear about the outside world.

00:21:31.700 --> 00:21:33.830
I bet she's too busy having fun out there.

00:21:33.910 --> 00:21:35.250
I sure hope so.

00:21:35.870 --> 00:21:37.120
Hey, you bums.

00:21:38.290 --> 00:21:40.090
This isn't the time to be flirting.

00:21:40.590 --> 00:21:42.590
You don't even have proper tits yet.

00:21:43.170 --> 00:21:44.840
You haven't even had your period, right?

00:21:44.970 --> 00:21:46.970
Listen up. No matter how talented you are,

00:21:47.050 --> 00:21:50.180
a chick who can't get pregnant
won't be chosen.

00:21:50.260 --> 00:21:52.850
You bastard! You fucking asshole!

00:21:53.810 --> 00:21:55.230
Fuck you!

00:21:56.390 --> 00:21:58.310
<i>I was thrown into solitary as punishment.</i>

00:22:00.150 --> 00:22:02.020
<i>We called it the "Red Room."</i>

00:22:02.360 --> 00:22:06.200
<i>It was actually part of a device used to
shred livestock to create fertilizer.</i>

00:22:06.490 --> 00:22:09.160
Blood... Bones... Brains?

00:22:12.830 --> 00:22:14.290
A human...

00:22:17.540 --> 00:22:19.000
Nobara...

00:22:20.670 --> 00:22:23.250
I thought Nobara went
to the outside world...

00:22:23.800 --> 00:22:25.970
She should be having fun out there...
